                        "entry_id": "8c127693-7d87-31c3-8cc7-369180432bc5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The fortified tower and main residence of a motte or early castle; a keep."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "24f3c071-f15a-4f54-94b7-4e58a1060aeb",
                                "sense_id": "6ea0f595-be3d-3840-a34c-5bfd374e81db",
                                "text": "It was a fortress of no great size, consisting of a donjon, or large and high square tower, surrounded by buildings of inferior height, which were encircled by an inner court-yard."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "71df0da8-ea3a-4510-9121-fba4407cbc36",
                                "sense_id": "6ea0f595-be3d-3840-a34c-5bfd374e81db",
                                "text": "[…] the prison fortress called Qomr, a mound of yellowish brick rising up from the left back of the turbid river, in whose donjon by long tradition the warlord was obliged to lay his head."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
